.TH FD_PUSH 3 "2023-04-15" "Fd Library"
.SH NAME
fd_push \- Push an (fd) to the top of the fdtable
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <fd.h>
.IR struct fd * fd_push(struct fd * d, int n, int mode);
nf
.SH DESCRIPTION
The function \(aqfd_push\(aq pushes a file descriptor \(d\) with index \(n\) and mode \(mode\) to the top of the \(fdtable\).
The function initializes the \(fd\) structure using \(fd_init\), sets the position in the \(fdtable\), links the \(fd\) in the \(fdtable\) and the \(fdstack\), and returns a pointer to the \(fd\).

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns a pointer to the pushed \(fd\).
If an error occurs, it returns NULL.
.SH ERRORS
No specific errors are expected from this function.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.B fd_push(fd, 10, O_RDONLY);
nf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fd_init (3),
.BR fdtable (3),
.BR fdstack (3).
